+# Specification Quality Checklist: Verify GraphHelm CLI on Windows 11 ARM64
+
+**Purpose**: Validate specification completeness and quality before proceeding to planning
+**Created**: 2026-10-26
+**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md)
+
+## Content Quality
+
+- [x] No implementation details (languages, frameworks, APIs)
+- [x] Focused on user value and business needs
+- [x] Written for non-technical stakeholders
+- [x] All mandatory sections completed
+
+## Requirement Completeness
+
+- [x] No [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers remain
+- [x] Requirements are testable and unambiguous
+- [x] Success criteria are measurable
+- [x] Success criteria are technology-agnostic (no implementation details)
+- [x] All acceptance scenarios are defined
+- [x] Edge cases are identified
+- [x] Scope is clearly bounded
+- [x] Dependencies and assumptions identified
+
+## Feature Readiness
+
+- [x] All functional requirements have clear acceptance criteria
+- [x] User scenarios cover primary flows
+- [x] Feature meets measurable outcomes defined in Success Criteria
+- [x] No implementation details leak into specification
+
+## Notes
+
+- Items marked incomplete require spec updates before `/speckit.clarify` or `/speckit.plan`
+- Validation iteration 1 (2026-10-26): all items pass on first review.
+- Judgment calls recorded during validation:
+  - "No implementation details": requirements name the documented command `graphhelm --version`,
+    the file `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`, and `systeminfo` as evidence examples. These are
+    accepted because the feature IS the execution of a documented journey and a documentation
+    change; they identify what is verified where, not how it is implemented. FR-003 marks the
+    `systeminfo` identity "for example" to keep the check method-agnostic.
+  - "Technology-agnostic success criteria": SC-002/SC-003 reference the documented CLI command
+    and its output because the user-facing contract of this feature is precisely that command; no
+    framework, language, or build-system detail is asserted.
+  - Key Entities section omitted: the feature involves no persistent user data (verification,
+    documentation, and an evidence transcript only), per template guidance to remove sections that
+    do not apply.
+  - Zero [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers: every open decision had a reasonable default, which is
+    recorded in Assumptions (ARM64 native vs. emulated, archives out of scope, doc edit limited to
+    GETTING_STARTED.md plus transcript, English-only prose, x86-64 host environment fact, skipped
+    extension hooks / fixed feature directory).
+  - Known limitation carried into planning, not a spec defect: the ARM64 run promise cannot be
+    observed from this checkout's x86-64 host; the Assumptions section records the environment
+    measurement and the `OBSERVER_MISSING` consequence so planning does not mistake a proxy for a
+    proof.
