+# Contract: Windows 11 ARM64 install journey (on-device)
+
+**Feature**: [../spec.md](../spec.md) | **Plan**: [../plan.md](../plan.md)
+
+This is the fixed command sequence the verification session executes on the device. It has two
+parts with different legal force:
+
+- **Part A — Journey (documented).** These commands are copied from
+  [`docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`](../../../docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md) (Prerequisites,
+  Windows commands, plus section 1, Windows block) **as written in the file under test**. They are
+  the promise: FR-001 succeeds only if Part A, alone, yields a working `graphhelm`. If the
+  document and this contract disagree at run time, the document wins — the session verifies the
+  document, not its mirror here.
+- **Part B — Evidence capture.** Commands added by this feature to establish the identities FR-003
+  demands (research R1/R2). They observe; they do not install. Their output goes to the transcript
+  ([evidence-transcript.md](evidence-transcript.md)).
+
+Environment: one fresh PowerShell session on the device, cloned repository at an arbitrary depth;
+`C:\path\to\GraphHelm` below means the clone root. Every command is recorded with its exit code.
+
+## Part A — Journey (exactly as documented; do not reorder or shorten)
+
+```powershell
+# A0. Prerequisites check (documented Checks column)
+cargo +1.97.1 --version        # only if the toolchain already exists; otherwise A1 installs it
+git --version
+
+# A1. Install the toolchain when missing (Prerequisites, Windows block)
+winget install --id Rustlang.Rustup --exact --source winget --accept-source-agreements --accept-package-agreements
+$env:Path = "$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin;$env:Path"
+rustup toolchain install 1.97.1 --profile minimal --component rustfmt clippy
+
+# A2. Section 1 — clone and build-or-install (Windows block)
+git clone https://github.com/stabem/GraphHelm.git
+cd GraphHelm
+cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path apps/cli
+graphhelm --version            # Expected last line, per the document: graphhelm 0.1.0
+```
+
+Notes fixed by the spec (edge cases):
+
+- **PATH refresh**: if `graphhelm` is not found immediately after A2, the only sanctioned remedy is
+  the documented one (new shell / PATH refresh) — no other step may be invented.
+- **Undocumented step rule**: any additional command required for success (a missing MSVC linker,
+  a toolchain host re-point per research R3, an archive substitution) fails SC-001 as written and
+  must be flagged in the transcript as a documentation defect whose fix lands in
+  GETTING_STARTED.md (in scope) before the claim is published.
+- **Archive path is out of scope**: the 0.1.0 release archives are x86-64 only; an ARM64 user who
+  took an archive instead of the source build has not run this journey.
+
+## Part B — Evidence capture (fixed expectations; see research R1/R2/R6)
+
+```powershell
+# B1. OS identity — must establish Windows 11 + ARM64 from the OS, never from a shell variable
+systeminfo | Select-String -Pattern 'OS Name|OS Version|System type'   # expect: ... ARM-based PC
+(Get-CimInstance Win32_Processor).Name                                  # expected: Snapdragon-class ARM name
+$PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString()                                    # context line for the transcript (not proof)
+
+# B2. Commit under test (A2 clone, unmodified)
+git rev-parse HEAD
+
+# B3. Toolchain identity — after A1, before A2's build
+rustup --version
+rustc --version --verbose        # the host: line MUST read aarch64-pc-windows-msvc (V2)
+
+# B4. Binary identity (optional direct check, R2) — after A2's install
+dumpbin /headers "$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin\graphhelm.exe"   # if present: expect machine (AArch64)
+# or, without dumpbin, the 2-byte PE machine field of graphhelm.exe at offset (DWORD@0x3C)+4 == AA64h
+# if no inspector exists, record that fact — B3 alone establishes the build (V2)
+
+# B5. Version baseline comparison input
+graphhelm --version; echo "exit=$LASTEXITCODE"                    # must be exit=0 (SC-002), line recorded verbatim
+```
+
+Fallback fixed in advance (research R3): if B3 reports `host: x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`, execute
+`rustup set default-host aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, reinstall the pinned toolchain, re-run B3, and
+flag the extra step as a documentation defect (V3). The journey then continues from A2 with the
+native toolchain in place.
+
+## Disqualifiers (any one voids the observation, FR-003 / spec edge cases)
+
+| Disqualifier | Detected by |
+|---|---|
+| OS not ARM64 (or identity taken from a shell variable only) | B1 lacks `ARM-based PC` (and no Snapdragon CPU name) |
+| Executed binary is x86-64 (incl. running emulated) | B3 host triple not `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`; B4 PE machine not AArch64 when checked |
+| Install needed an undocumented step | Part A list extended without a V3 flag + doc fix |
+| `graphhelm --version` needed a retry or failed | B5 exit code / first-invocation requirement |
+| Run performed in cross-compilation or under full OS emulation from another host | provenance note in the transcript header |
+
+A disqualified run is still recorded — as `recorded_fail` (data model Entity 1) with its cause —
+and never counted toward the verified-platform claim (FR-007).
