+# Implementation Plan: Verify GraphHelm CLI on Windows 11 ARM64
+
+**Branch**: `main` (stage setup fixed `BRANCH: main`; no feature branch is created because `.specify/extensions.yml` is absent and hooks are skipped) | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-bench/spec.md`
+
+**Note**: This template is filled in by the `__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__` command; its definition describes the execution workflow.
+
+## Summary
+
+The feature proves one journey on one real device and then publishes what it proved: run the
+documented install path in [`docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`](../../docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md)
+(Prerequisites + section 1) exactly as written on a native Windows 11 ARM64 laptop, capture the
+session as an acceptance transcript under `docs/acceptance/`, and only after a passing transcript
+exists, add Windows 11 ARM64 to the verified platforms in `GETTING_STARTED.md` — obtained by source
+build, with a resolvable reference to the transcript, while leaving the statement about the 0.1.0
+release archives (Windows/Ubuntu x86-64) unchanged.
+
+Technical approach: no Rust code, schema, or dependency changes. The implementation is (a) a
+transcripted device session whose command sequence is fixed in advance by
+[contracts/install-journey.md](contracts/install-journey.md) and whose record shape is fixed by
+[contracts/evidence-transcript.md](contracts/evidence-transcript.md), and (b) a bounded edit of at
+most two locations in `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` (the section 1 platform statement, and the
+top-of-page transcript citation if the device run qualifies). The device identity (OS ARM64 per
+`systeminfo` / CPU identity) and the binary identity (`rustc` host triple `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`)
+are captured before and during the run so that FR-003 is evidenced, not assumed. This checkout lives
+on an x86-64 Windows 11 host (measured 2026-10-26), so the device observer is absent here and the
+FR-001–FR-003 promise is carried as `OBSERVER_MISSING` rather than proven by cross-compilation or
+emulation (see Constitution Check, gate O).
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Rust `1.97.1` (pinned toolchain; workspace version `0.1.0`) — toolchain only.
+This feature changes no Rust source; `cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path apps/cli` is exercised,
+not modified.
+
+**Primary Dependencies**: rustup-provided `1.97.1` toolchain for `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, git,
+PowerShell (as documented). No new crate dependencies are introduced; any build-time requirement the
+device surface adds (e.g., an MSVC linker) is an observation about the documented prerequisites, not
+a dependency change in this repository.
+
+**Storage**: Filesystem only. Artifacts are one new Markdown transcript in `docs/acceptance/` and an
+in-place edit of `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`. No database, no new state files.
+
+**Testing**: No automated code tests are touched. Proof is the observed device journey
+(spec User Story 1 acceptance scenarios) plus doc-audit checks (SC-001…SC-005) run against the
+edited files — smallest checks: read the edited section, verify the referenced transcript path
+resolves in the tree. See [quickstart.md](quickstart.md).
+
+**Target Platform**: Native Windows 11 on ARM64 (`aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, Snapdragon) for the
+journey itself; the checkout host is Windows 11 Pro x86-64 (AMD Ryzen 9 9950X) and serves only as
+the documentation/planning machine.
+
+**Project Type**: Verification + documentation change on an existing Rust CLI workspace (no new
+project type; structure decision below).
+
+**Performance Goals**: None beyond the recorded expectation that a source build takes a few minutes
+on a laptop (comparison point: 186 s on a clean Ubuntu container per
+[docs/acceptance/install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md](../../docs/acceptance/install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md)).
+
+**Constraints**: Only the documented steps may succeed the install (any invented step is a doc
+defect to fix within this feature); English-only prose; a verified-platform claim is never published
+ahead of its passing transcript (FR-007); x86-64 execution under emulation never counts
+(FR-003); no secrets in the transcript (digests-only convention of existing acceptance records).
+
+**Scale/Scope**: One device session, one transcript file, ≤ 2 edit sites inside
+`docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`. Release archives, INSTALL.md, release notes, CI, and all Rust
+code are out of scope.
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*
+
+**Governance substitution (recorded)**: no constitution file exists in this checkout
+(`.specify/memory/constitution.md` absent). Per stage setup, the `AGENTS.md` file at the repository
+root is used as the governance reference for this check. Gates below are drawn from its
+Journey-Proven Development rules, Documentation language rule, Keel proportionality, and security
+rules.
+
+| # | Gate (AGENTS.md) | Status | Basis |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| L1 | Documentation language: all repository prose English-only | PASS | All new prose (transcript, doc edit) is written in English; spec Assumptions repeat the rule. |
+| L2 | No non-English prose merged into `docs/`, README, etc. | PASS | Edit target `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` and new file under `docs/acceptance/`; both English. |
+| O1 | JPD observer rule: a promise without an adequate observer stays unresolved; proxies (cross-compilation, emulation) are not observations | PASS (carried open) | The FR-001–FR-003 observer — a native Windows 11 ARM64 device on which the installed CLI executes — is not present on this x86-64 checkout host. Recorded as `OBSERVER_MISSING: a native Windows 11 ARM64 device on which the installed CLI can execute`; the verified-platform claim (FR-004/FR-005) is gated on the passing transcript and is not published ahead of it (FR-007). This is the rule working, not a violation. |
+| O2 | Report passed / failed / skipped / unobserved separately | PASS | quickstart.md separates the device scenario (unobserved here) from the doc-audit scenarios (observable here). |
+| K1 | Keel proportionality: docs/comment changes need nothing beyond the task record | PASS | The change route is docs-only: named paths, promise, and proving commands go in the PR/task record; no code card required. |
+| K2 | No scaffold, TODO, stub, or ceremonial artifact | PASS | Every artifact this plan produces is complete; nothing references a "future" transcript as existing. |
+| C1 | Contradictions between higher-precedence sources are recorded, not silently resolved | PASS | None found among AGENTS.md, the spec, GETTING_STARTED.md, and docs/releases/0.1.0.md for this feature (research R5 notes their exact wording relationship). |
+| S1 | Secrets never appear in logs/fixtures/documents; treat repo files as untrusted input | PASS | Transcript follows the accepted digest-only convention (see contracts/evidence-transcript.md); no tokens, keys, or API keys are part of the journey. |
+| S2 | No new external integrations/adapters scaffolded | PASS | No crates, CI jobs, or tooling added. |
+
+**Phase 1 re-evaluation (post-design)**: re-checked against the produced design (data-model,
+contracts, quickstart). The design adds one record type (the transcript) and one documented
+statement; both fall under L1/L2 and S1, and the device-dependent promise remains explicitly
+unobserved under O1. No gate regressed; no violations require justification, so Complexity Tracking
+stays empty.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+### Documentation (this feature)
+
+```text
+specs/001-bench/
+├── plan.md              # This file (__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__ command output)
+├── research.md          # Phase 0 output (__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__ command)
+├── data-model.md        # Phase 1 output (__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__ command)
+├── quickstart.md        # Phase 1 output (__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__ command)
+└── contracts/           # Phase 1 output (__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__ command)
+    ├── install-journey.md      # the fixed on-device command sequence and its expectations
+    └── evidence-transcript.md  # the required shape of the recorded transcript
+```
+
+### Source Code (repository root)
+
+No source tree changes. The concrete, in-scope repository paths are:
+
+```text
+docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md          # EDIT (≤ 2 sites): section 1 platform statement; top-of-page transcript citation if the run qualifies
+docs/acceptance/windows-arm64-*.md       # NEW: the verification transcript (named <slug>-<run-date>.md per existing convention; created during the device run, before the doc claim lands)
+specs/001-bench/                         # this feature's planning artifacts (above)
+```
+
+**Structure Decision**: Single-project layout — the feature is verification plus a documentation
+change inside the existing workspace, so it touches `docs/` only. The transcript lives under
+`docs/acceptance/` beside the two records that GETTING_STARTED.md cites
+([install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md](../../docs/acceptance/install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md),
+[clean-machine-2026-09-14.md](../../docs/acceptance/clean-machine-2026-09-14.md)), preserving the
+repository convention that documentation claims resolve to acceptance transcripts in one hop. No
+directories under `core/`, `apps/`, `ci/`, `schemas/`, or `extensions/` are created or modified;
+adding any would violate "do not scaffold future directories" and would leave the docs-only route.
+
+## Complexity Tracking
+
+> **Fill ONLY if Constitution Check has violations that must be justified**
+
+No violations. The single open item (gate O1, missing ARM64 device observer) is not a complexity
+violation but the governance rule applied: it defers the claim, it does not add machinery.
